# drizzle journals every migration by sha256 of the file's raw bytes, so a
# checkout whose line endings differ makes an already-applied migration look
# pending - and `migrate` then re-applies it and fails. With core.autocrlf=true
# a Windows checkout gets CRLF while CI and Railway get LF, which is how this
# repo ended up with 8 migrations journaled under CRLF hashes and 9 under LF.
# Pin SQL so every checkout agrees.
*.sql text eol=lf
